        {
          "id": 1983238832,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Windows has separate \"Make Text Size Bigger\" and \"Scale everything\" settings.\n\nIn the other issue, Guy said that \"[i]n macOS, the Display pane of System Preferences lets you increase (or decrease) text sizes; it affects Wireshark, including the filter box (I just tried it).\" I don't have a Mac though.\n\nThe \"Make Text Size Bigger\" requires restarting Wireshark if the value is changed to make everything look correct, whereas the scaling setting does not. Somewhat a separate issue from this, as this doesn't make anything worse and makes things a little better.\n\nI tested this and this seems like it works well, and the packet list header is associated with the packet list, so it makes sense.\n\nWould it make sense to also affect the main display filter (#16922)? Would the stock icons also adjust in size or would that require additional changes?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
